WEBVTT

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:07.470
I can't finish reading the magazine pages

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:14.380
I get the feeling that I must read it

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:21.130
Game cartridges are stacked in the corner of the room

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:27.830
Is there no meaning if I don't play them?

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:32.930
You're on the other side of the table

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:36.300
I'm talking to you, but...

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:43.230
You don't change your facial expression at all

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:49.480
Even though I'm this close to you

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:56.750
These feelings don't reach you, don't reach you

00:00:57.170 --> 00:01:03.490
What is truly precious?

00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:11.000
The spell card Black Luster Ritual!

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:17.890
Black Luster Ritual tributes monsters whose combined Levels equal 8.

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:25.460
One soul invites light!

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:27.930
Another soul guides darkness!

00:01:31.370 --> 00:01:35.820
The souls of light and dark create the light of chaos!

00:01:40.730 --> 00:01:41.560
What?

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:44.320
Black Luster Soldier descends!

00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:50.290
That's the legendary strongest warrior?

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:52.460
Chaos Blade!

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:01.570
Harpie's Pet Dragon is destroyed!

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:13.180
Brutal • Heavy Metal Deck

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:22.600
In the first match of the tournament between Yugi Muto and Mai Kujaku, Yugi Muto is the winner.

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:25.920
He moves on to the finals!

00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:27.360
All right!

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:28.460
You did it, Yugi!

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:33.930
Thank you, everyone... and my other self.

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:42.240
Congratulations, Yugi boy.

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:45.240
That was a wonderful duel.

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:46.980
That punk!

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:48.860
Pegasus!

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:57.540
In order to save Grandpa, Kaiba and Mokuba, I will win the finals and defeat you!

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:03.930
We'll now begin the second match of the tournament.

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:07.900
Keith Howard and Katsuya Jonouchi, proceed to the Ring.

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:10.900
All right, I'm up.

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:13.460
Listen, Jonouchi.  Stay calm.

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:16.700
Writing "person" on your palm three times gets rid of stage fright.

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:18.400
Be quiet!

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.080
You're making me more nervous!

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:22.400
Good luck, Jonouchi.

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:23.610
You better win.

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:26.620
I know.

00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:29.290
Like I said, write "person" three times...

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:31.800
Be quiet!  You're doing this on purpose!

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:34.300
What?  I'm being a friend!

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:36.500
Do you think he'll be okay?

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:37.960
Who knows?

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:43.700
Yugi.

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:45.500
Jonouchi.

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:50.570
Jonouchi?

00:03:50.780 --> 00:03:54.520
Yugi, I promise I'll win.

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:57.750
And when I do...

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:01.190
When you do, let's duel each other with all our strength.

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:06.490
Yeah.  I won't run or hide or take it easy on you.

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:09.000
We'll battle with all our strength!

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:15.140
Go, Jonouchi!

00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:16.200
Give it your best!

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:22.750
Keith isn't here.

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:26.050
I'm sleepy.

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:29.550
Keith, get in the Ring!

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:31.600
Huh?  What?

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:37.990
An amateur really intends to duel Bandit Keith?

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:42.660
I've already told you that I'll crush you with my cards.

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:46.100
You're going to crush me?

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:49.770
Show me your entry cards.

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:53.570
C'mon, kid.  Show him your card.

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:55.750
He's so arrogant...

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:58.240
Huh?

00:04:58.640 --> 00:04:59.940
Show me your card.

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:00.980
Right!

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:03.850
Huh?  I know it was in my jacket pocket.

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:07.480
Don't tell me Jonouchi lost his card!

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:09.660
When it comes to Jonouchi, that's a possibility.

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:10.620
That idiot!

00:05:10.900 --> 00:05:12.060
Hey!

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:16.720
That means he's now allowed to duel, right Pegasus?

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:19.750
Hold on!  I know I have it!

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:20.520
Correct.

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:24.940
If you do not have an entry card, you are disqualified.

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:27.370
Oh no...

00:05:28.650 --> 00:05:33.920
He's not going to find it because I stole this card from him.

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:38.480
I'll now make the finals without having to duel.

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:41.950
Jonouchi, maybe you dropped your card!

00:05:41.950 --> 00:05:44.490
I probably left it in my room.

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:46.680
I'll go get it.

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:48.290
You have five minutes.

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:49.660
What?

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:52.600
The second match begins in five minutes.

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:55.050
At 11 o'clock.

00:05:56.030 --> 00:06:01.970
If you fail to show me the entry card within five minutes, you will be disqualified.

00:06:03.410 --> 00:06:07.840
But five minutes is barely enough time to make it to his room and back!

00:06:08.060 --> 00:06:10.780
Rules are rules.  No exceptions.

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:16.520
Run, Jonouchi!

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:23.730
Damn!  I've made it this far, so I won't give up now!

00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:30.500
Are you sure that clock isn't running slow?

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:32.160
The clock is fine.

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:36.870
And if you're not at the Ring before the deadline, you'll also be disqualified.

00:06:37.150 --> 00:06:40.240
What?  How annoying.

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:46.140
Damn!  Where is it?

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:54.700
I gave my other card to Jonouchi, so I only have this card left.

00:06:54.700 --> 00:06:55.600
Hey!

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:59.250
Disqualify him already.

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:01.430
He won't be coming back anyway.

00:07:01.800 --> 00:07:02.820
What did you say?

00:07:02.820 --> 00:07:04.800
Why do you say that?

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:05.870
It's simple.

00:07:06.180 --> 00:07:08.870
He's a total amateur when it comes to cards.

00:07:08.870 --> 00:07:14.200
No matter how dumb he is, he knows that he can't defeat me.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:17.650
He actually doesn't want to duel.

00:07:18.050 --> 00:07:21.420
He pretended to lose his card so that he had an excuse to run away.

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:25.750
He's probably crying outside the castle.

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:27.020
You're wrong!

00:07:27.020 --> 00:07:27.960
What?

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:31.250
Jonouchi isn't the type who would run away!

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:35.800
He will definitely come back and duel you!

00:07:37.550 --> 00:07:39.500
I hope you're right.

00:07:40.450 --> 00:07:41.800
One minute left.

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:42.900
Oh no!

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:44.350
He won't make it in time.

00:07:44.350 --> 00:07:47.100
Damn!  What are you doing, Jonouchi?

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:48.740
Jonouchi...

00:07:56.600 --> 00:07:58.960
I couldn't find the entry card.

00:07:59.880 --> 00:08:05.080
I came to this island and kept winning, even if it was luck.

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:08.100
But my dream ends after I made it this far?

00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:11.540
Why am I such an idiot?

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:16.760
Shizuka, forgive me.

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:22.360
Stand up, Jonouchi!

00:08:23.550 --> 00:08:26.820
Save your tears of frustration after you lose a duel!

00:08:27.850 --> 00:08:29.750
It's a runny nose, not tears!

00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:34.690
It's not stopping.

00:08:34.690 --> 00:08:35.500
Here.

00:08:36.150 --> 00:08:38.640
Wipe your nose.  You look pathetic.

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:42.650
This handkerchief is wet.

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:46.450
Anzu told me about your little sister.

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:50.140
Jonouchi, don't abandon your wishes so quickly.

00:08:50.360 --> 00:08:56.140
Those tears for your sister - or was it a runny nose?  Well, that's irrelevant.

00:08:56.380 --> 00:08:59.280
I hope your wish comes true.

00:09:04.440 --> 00:09:05.350
This is...

00:09:06.240 --> 00:09:08.100
Wait, Mai!

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:10.790
I don't need it anymore.

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:14.520
Mai, why are you doing this for me?

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:16.560
You don't have time to waste!

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:17.330
Right!

00:09:17.720 --> 00:09:19.000
Jonouchi!

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:20.000
What is it?

00:09:20.850 --> 00:09:21.670
Win.

00:09:22.900 --> 00:09:24.110
Yeah!

00:09:25.850 --> 00:09:27.280
Why?

00:09:27.700 --> 00:09:30.000
Because we're friends.

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:34.340
Jonouchi!

00:09:43.820 --> 00:09:46.560
You've come back so that you can hear that you've been disqualified.

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:54.000
Here's my entry card.

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:55.170
Any problems?

00:09:59.380 --> 00:10:01.440
But I took his card!

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:05.220
You are allowed to enter the tournament.

00:10:05.480 --> 00:10:07.920
Whew.  He made us worry.

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:11.550
Keith, let's begin this duel.

00:10:12.300 --> 00:10:15.840
Fine.  It's a waste of my time, but I'll duel you.

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:18.640
But only hell awaits you.

00:10:18.640 --> 00:10:20.980
Then I'll defeat you in hell!

00:10:20.980 --> 00:10:22.230
You punk!

00:10:22.460 --> 00:10:28.440
The second match of the tournament between Keith Howard and Katsuya Jonouchi will now begin.

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:30.870
Go for it!

00:10:31.640 --> 00:10:34.100
Win, Jonouchi.

00:10:34.520 --> 00:10:36.140
Start the duel!

00:10:36.790 --> 00:10:37.950
Duel!

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:57.830
The second match of the tournament between Keith Howard and Katsuya Jonouchi will now begin.

00:10:57.830 --> 00:10:59.770
Start the duel!

00:11:04.180 --> 00:11:06.570
Win, Jonouchi.

00:11:07.850 --> 00:11:09.580
Prepare yourself.

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:14.520
The former American champion Bandit Keith will use his mighty deck to send you to hell.

00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:18.150
That title is meaningless here.

00:11:18.150 --> 00:11:21.690
I made it this far after finishing 8th in the regionals.

00:11:22.540 --> 00:11:24.690
That kid needs to watch his mouth.

00:11:25.180 --> 00:11:26.300
My turn.

00:11:26.300 --> 00:11:28.300
I play this in defense position.

00:11:31.450 --> 00:11:32.800
It's started.

00:11:32.800 --> 00:11:34.940
This is going to be a tough duel.

00:11:34.940 --> 00:11:39.250
Don't worry.  He's already won tough duels to get here.

00:11:39.250 --> 00:11:42.300
Jonouchi, we have your back!

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:45.000
Do it!  You're not an amateur anymore!

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:47.110
You can do it, Jonouchi!

00:11:47.110 --> 00:11:49.100
Thanks, everyone.

00:11:49.380 --> 00:11:50.750
Watch me.

00:11:50.750 --> 00:11:55.560
I promise to win and use the prize money to repair Shizuka's eyes.

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:59.490
I also play a monster in defense position and end my turn.

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:04.680
I know that your deck only contains weak monsters.

00:12:05.150 --> 00:12:05.970
I'll destroy it!

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:08.770
Pendulum Machine in attack position!

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:14.510
A Machine monster?

00:12:14.740 --> 00:12:18.680
Go!  Destroy his defending monster in a bloodbath!

00:12:23.250 --> 00:12:24.540
Battle Warrior!

00:12:24.540 --> 00:12:25.350
Do it.

00:12:25.820 --> 00:12:27.220
Conviction Execution!

00:12:31.340 --> 00:12:32.560
Jonouchi...

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:34.460
This is fine.

00:12:34.880 --> 00:12:40.600
Jonouchi used Battle Warrior as a decoy to draw his opponent's card into attack position.

00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:44.780
So that he can play a more powerful monster on his next turn.

00:12:45.040 --> 00:12:48.040
Keith uses Machine monsters?

00:12:48.260 --> 00:12:49.480
Why?

00:12:49.480 --> 00:12:51.650
Hey, it's your turn.

00:12:51.860 --> 00:12:54.150
You don't have a single set card.

00:12:54.150 --> 00:12:55.820
That carelessness will cost you.

00:12:56.250 --> 00:13:01.290
Go!  Giltia the D. Knight in attack position!

00:13:01.500 --> 00:13:02.200
All right!

00:13:02.200 --> 00:13:05.800
Jonouchi's card has higher attack points.

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:08.980
Here I go!  Soul Spear!

00:13:12.620 --> 00:13:13.800
What?

00:13:13.800 --> 00:13:15.200
The attack didn't work?

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:17.500
No way!  Why?

00:13:17.510 --> 00:13:20.250
What's going on, Yugi?

00:13:21.180 --> 00:13:22.860
You fell for it.

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:27.610
All my Machine monsters have magic-resistant armor.

00:13:28.140 --> 00:13:30.920
Magical attacks don't work on them.

00:13:31.140 --> 00:13:33.920
I see.  That's why he chose Machine monsters.

00:13:33.920 --> 00:13:39.450
Magic-based monsters and attacks using spell cards won't work.

00:13:39.450 --> 00:13:41.860
Damn!  Do something, Jonouchi!

00:13:42.700 --> 00:13:44.030
It's my turn.

00:13:44.450 --> 00:13:47.830
Launcher Spider!

00:13:52.060 --> 00:13:53.820
Another Machine monster.

00:13:53.820 --> 00:13:56.310
He keeps bringing out those ugly monsters.

00:13:57.290 --> 00:13:58.280
Do it.

00:14:01.080 --> 00:14:02.300
Damn!

00:14:04.020 --> 00:14:05.500
How was that, punk?

00:14:05.500 --> 00:14:08.260
You're not worthy of being my opponent.

00:14:09.320 --> 00:14:12.420
He's tough.  That's why he was the former American champ.

00:14:12.420 --> 00:14:15.730
He plays one powerful card after another.

00:14:15.940 --> 00:14:17.040
Incredible.

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:19.980
The power of those Machine monsters is on a whole different level.

00:14:20.550 --> 00:14:22.550
He can still win, right Yugi?

00:14:22.550 --> 00:14:27.910
Keith's deck is a heavyweight power deck made up mostly of Machine cards.

00:14:28.640 --> 00:14:33.850
He stops all magic attacks and uses overwhelming power to defeat his opponents.

00:14:34.080 --> 00:14:39.290
But he has to rely on straightforward attacks to make best use of that power.

00:14:40.140 --> 00:14:43.200
So that's where you can find a weakness to exploit.

00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:48.660
I can't fight him head-on with these cards.

00:14:49.150 --> 00:14:52.920
I set one card and play a monster in defense position.

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:55.650
I'm sure it's another weak monster.

00:14:56.920 --> 00:15:02.910
Even if I destroy that weakling in defense position, I can't damage his life points.

00:15:02.910 --> 00:15:08.350
Instead, I'll catch that idiot in a trap and quickly win this match.

00:15:08.700 --> 00:15:11.280
I also set a card.

00:15:11.280 --> 00:15:13.200
And I place this in defense-

00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:19.860
Oops, it slipped out of my hand.

00:15:20.420 --> 00:15:23.800
I set this monster in defense position and end my turn.

00:15:24.180 --> 00:15:26.580
I saw another ugly monster for a moment.

00:15:26.580 --> 00:15:27.830
What was that?

00:15:28.150 --> 00:15:30.500
I saw what it was, Keith.

00:15:30.500 --> 00:15:33.400
It wasn't a Machine monster.

00:15:33.400 --> 00:15:37.780
It was Zoa.  Since it's Dark Attribute, it's not resistant to magic.

00:15:38.460 --> 00:15:39.850
Flame Swordsman.

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:42.550
I drew a nice card.

00:15:42.550 --> 00:15:43.280
I can win with this.

00:15:43.580 --> 00:15:45.350
It's your chance!

00:15:45.350 --> 00:15:46.960
Go, Jonouchi!

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:48.000
Something's wrong.

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:48.960
What's wrong?

00:15:49.540 --> 00:15:51.800
Flame Swordsman in attack position!

00:15:54.280 --> 00:15:59.000
Zoa has 2600 attack points and 1900 defense points.

00:15:59.400 --> 00:16:00.580
So?

00:16:01.100 --> 00:16:01.930
I see.

00:16:02.200 --> 00:16:04.240
And I'll add a spell card.

00:16:04.240 --> 00:16:10.000
We were focused on its magic resistance that we forgot that Zoa had more attack points than defense points.

00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:13.410
The fact that he played it in defense position means he's trying to lure Jonouchi.

00:16:13.720 --> 00:16:14.850
Salamandra!

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:18.280
Flame Swordsman gains 700 attack points!

00:16:18.520 --> 00:16:21.520
That means he dropped his card on purpose!

00:16:21.520 --> 00:16:22.320
Jonouchi!

00:16:22.320 --> 00:16:23.220
Battle!

00:16:25.120 --> 00:16:26.060
You fool.

00:16:26.380 --> 00:16:28.040
I activate my trap card.

00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:28.780
What?

00:16:29.060 --> 00:16:31.500
Magic Metal Force!

00:16:32.200 --> 00:16:36.560
It turns my monster into metal, raising both its attack and defense points by 400.

00:16:36.800 --> 00:16:38.150
Turn into metal?

00:16:38.150 --> 00:16:40.500
It does more than turn it into metal.

00:16:40.500 --> 00:16:46.030
Magic Metal Force reflects magic attacks back at you!

00:16:46.030 --> 00:16:47.320
What?

00:16:51.660 --> 00:16:52.990
Flame Swordsman!

00:16:58.620 --> 00:17:01.720
You fell for such a simple trap.

00:17:01.720 --> 00:17:03.730
You really are an amateur.

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:05.660
Jonouchi...

00:17:05.880 --> 00:17:06.970
My turn.

00:17:08.800 --> 00:17:10.760
You're done, kid.

00:17:10.760 --> 00:17:11.440
What?

00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:18.360
I'll use this card to draw out your monster in defense position.

00:17:18.360 --> 00:17:20.180
That's Stop Defense!

00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:25.050
Axe Raider?

00:17:25.280 --> 00:17:29.560
That weak monster is a fitting end for you.

00:17:30.220 --> 00:17:31.020
This is bad!

00:17:31.020 --> 00:17:35.020
If he takes Metalzoa's attack, Jonouchi will lose!

00:17:35.020 --> 00:17:35.890
Jonouchi!

00:17:36.100 --> 00:17:38.140
It's game over.

00:17:38.140 --> 00:17:41.330
Metalzoa, attack Axe Raider!

00:17:45.400 --> 00:17:47.570
Metalzoa vanished?

00:17:48.920 --> 00:17:49.690
That's...

00:17:50.430 --> 00:17:51.460
What?

00:17:51.880 --> 00:17:56.820
How's that!  I activate the trap card Chasm of Spikes!

00:17:56.820 --> 00:17:59.250
What?  A trap card?

00:17:59.250 --> 00:18:01.690
You're incredible, Jonouchi!

00:18:02.060 --> 00:18:10.560
Not only does it destroy Metalzoa, Keith loses a quarter of its attack points, which is 750 life points!

00:18:10.780 --> 00:18:12.260
What's wrong, Keith?

00:18:12.260 --> 00:18:17.340
The former American champ is nothing special because he falls for such a simple trap.

00:18:17.340 --> 00:18:18.770
That punk!

00:18:19.100 --> 00:18:20.500
I can't believe it.

00:18:20.500 --> 00:18:24.780
Jonouchi is battling the former American champion on equal footing.

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:28.060
There's a flow to every duel.

00:18:28.060 --> 00:18:31.720
Whoever captures the flow will win in the end.

00:18:31.950 --> 00:18:36.450
Jonouchi has the natural instinct to capture the flow.

00:18:37.480 --> 00:18:40.480
The tide has turned in Jonouchi's favor.

00:18:40.480 --> 00:18:42.860
All right!  Go, Jonouchi!

00:18:43.080 --> 00:18:44.280
My turn.

00:18:44.280 --> 00:18:46.500
First, I set one card.

00:18:46.500 --> 00:18:49.570
Keith, this is a trap card, so be careful.

00:18:49.800 --> 00:18:52.180
He's getting confident!

00:18:52.180 --> 00:18:55.010
I hope he doesn't get too carried away and make a mistake.

00:18:55.010 --> 00:18:56.700
How dare you make fun of me!

00:18:56.700 --> 00:19:00.810
Your trickery won't work on me in a million years!

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:04.250
I switch Axe Raider back to defense position.

00:19:04.780 --> 00:19:07.190
And I place this in attack position.

00:19:07.980 --> 00:19:11.620
Garoozis, attack Pendulum Machine!

00:19:12.670 --> 00:19:13.560
Battle!

00:19:20.120 --> 00:19:20.870
Damn!

00:19:21.100 --> 00:19:22.620
What's the matter, Keith?

00:19:22.620 --> 00:19:25.670
You're not living up to your title as the former #1 American duelist.

00:19:25.670 --> 00:19:27.010
Silence, punk!

00:19:27.550 --> 00:19:30.340
Launcher Spider, pulverize Garoozis!

00:19:34.560 --> 00:19:36.700
It was blown away until there was nothing left.

00:19:36.700 --> 00:19:38.420
Not good enough, Keith.

00:19:38.420 --> 00:19:41.120
My trap card has already activated.

00:19:41.120 --> 00:19:41.790
What?

00:19:42.760 --> 00:19:44.460
Kunai with Chain!

00:19:44.460 --> 00:19:48.360
It becomes an Equip Card, raising its attack points by 500!

00:19:48.360 --> 00:19:50.300
Go, Garoozis!

00:19:50.600 --> 00:19:52.230
Axe Crush!

00:19:57.100 --> 00:19:58.160
He did it!

00:19:58.160 --> 00:20:01.540
It's only a slight difference, but Jonouchi has taken the lead!

00:20:01.760 --> 00:20:04.280
I never knew Jonouchi was this strong!

00:20:04.580 --> 00:20:09.950
His cards know about Jonouchi's desire to save his sister.

00:20:10.160 --> 00:20:11.620
Nice, Jonouchi!

00:20:11.940 --> 00:20:14.550
You're the best today!

00:20:16.660 --> 00:20:20.490
Why am I having trouble with this amateur?

00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:23.080
Too bad, Keith.

00:20:23.080 --> 00:20:26.940
It seems you're the one who's going to fall into hell!

00:20:32.920 --> 00:20:36.100
You're doing well, Jonouchi!  You can win!

00:20:36.100 --> 00:20:41.650
With your Time Wizard-Baby Dragon combo, Keith's Machine monsters are instantly pulverized!

00:20:41.650 --> 00:20:44.350
What?  He beat your Time Magic?

00:20:44.350 --> 00:20:47.750
He used Time Machine to bring back a monster from the previous turn?

00:20:47.750 --> 00:20:51.050
Hang in there, Jonouchi!  Don't give up hope!

00:20:51.050 --> 00:20:55.400
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Transcend Time!
Red-Eyes Black Metal Dragon

00:20:55.400 --> 00:20:57.000
Duel, standby!

00:21:01.330 --> 00:21:09.760
The flask glistens

00:21:10.790 --> 00:21:17.600
Wait for me in the science classroom

00:21:18.100 --> 00:21:26.570
If we put our cold hands together

00:21:27.270 --> 00:21:34.350
And rub them together, they become warm

00:21:36.050 --> 00:21:40.180
Shower of happiness

00:21:40.470 --> 00:21:44.290
I will shower you with it

00:21:44.620 --> 00:21:52.570
I will support you even when you feel lonely

00:21:52.770 --> 00:21:56.800
Shower of happiness

00:21:57.070 --> 00:22:00.930
You are not alone

00:22:01.310 --> 00:22:07.650
You're protected by a giant ring of friendship
